--   settings.automation_timezone); one push of an invoice at a time; an
--   invoice number Xero has for another customer,
--   amount or invoice is not taken over; a connection let go begins what was
--   under way again (_xero_tasks_restart) and its late answers are not
--   applied; pg_net is used only where this database may use its queue and
--   answers (_xero_net_state); the sign-in's state names the portal, so the
--   portal goes straight to Xero (rpc_xero_connect_start takes its origin);
--   links from before are given their organisation where only one was ever
--   connected, and where it is not known are kept, read back, and asked of
--   Xero before a push or a void (the 'probe' step); a person's no to
--   recording a payment stands over every push of the invoice waiting
--   (rpc_xero_push_now's p_payment); what is marked sent or paid while a
--   connection has ended without the firm choosing it (the trigger, on
--   status and paid_at) waits for the next one, unless an administrator lets
--   it go (rpc_xero_discard_waiting, which lets go the calls still out for it
--   too); a call of a push no longer under way is not sent (_xero_build), nor
--   is one still out from an organisation's last connection taken up when it
--   is connected again (_xero_apply_connect); and on the upgrade a connection
--   made through Pental's earlier app is ended, to connect again, and what
--   was marked in the thirty days before and never queued is queued, marking
--   by marking as the automatic-push switches say.
-- 2025100310 (follow-up 1837): scanning from the firm's own side: a
